---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'

const requirements = [
  ['Docker', 'To run the published container image.'],
  ['PostgreSQL 16+', 'Required specifically — not SQLite or MySQL. Plugin isolation is enforced with row-level security, roles and schemas that only Postgres has.'],
  ['A place to put it', 'A homelab box, a small VPS, anything that can stay reachable. Wicker Money doesn’t need much: it’s a single container plus your existing Postgres.'],
]
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Self-hosting"
  description="What it actually takes to run Wicker Money yourself: Docker, PostgreSQL 16+, and why Postgres specifically is a hard requirement."
>
  <section class="wmm-section wmm-page-hero">
    <div class="wmm-container">
      <p class="wmm-eyebrow">Self-hosting</p>
      <h1>Run it on your own server.</h1>
      <p class="wmm-lede">
        This page is the honest overview. The
        <a href="https://wickermoney.dev/docs/self-hosting/quickstart">step-by-step quickstart</a>
        lives on the docs site and is the one that's kept current line-by-line —
        this page won't repeat it in full and drift out of sync.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wmm-section wmm-section--alt">
    <div class="wmm-container">
      <h2>What you need</h2>
      <table>
        <tbody>
          {requirements.map(([name, note]) => (
            <tr>
              <td style="width: 220px; font-weight: 600;">{name}</td>
              <td>{note}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wmm-section">
    <div class="wmm-container">
      <h2>Why Postgres is a hard requirement</h2>
      <p class="wmm-lede" style="max-width: 72ch;">
        The core owns identity and the ledger; everything that interprets money —
        budgets, forecasting, importers — is a plugin. Keeping one plugin's
        data invisible to another (and to the wrong user) is enforced with Postgres
        row-level security and per-plugin database roles derived from each plugin's
        manifest, not just checked in application code. That's a deliberate,
        load-bearing choice, not a default nobody reconsidered.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wmm-section wmm-section--alt">
    <div class="wmm-container">
      <h2>The shape of it</h2>
      <ol class="wmm-steps wmm-steps--wide">
        <li><strong>Pull the image.</strong> <code>docker pull ghcr.io/wickermoney/wicker-money:latest</code> — pin a version once you have plugins in the picture; bundled plugins ship inside the same image.</li>
        <li><strong>Point it at Postgres.</strong> The app connects as a least-privilege role that owns nothing and can't bypass row-level security. Migrations connect as a separate owner role that can. Both point at the same database.</li>
        <li><strong>Run migrations.</strong> The image doesn't migrate on start, on purpose — that would mean the running API needs owner credentials, which it deliberately doesn't have.</li>
        <li><strong>Start it.</strong> <code>docker compose up -d</code>. Put a reverse proxy in front if you want TLS and a real domain; set <code>TRUST_PROXY=true</code> if you do.</li>
        <li><strong>Sign up first.</strong> The first account on an instance is its owner &mdash; the one who can turn plugins on and off. Anyone who signs up after you is a member, with their own data. From v0.5.0 you can set <code>BOOTSTRAP_OWNER_EMAIL</code> to your address so that someone who registers before you doesn't become the owner. Addresses aren't verified, so register promptly either way. Once everyone who needs an account has one, set <code>REGISTRATION_ENABLED=false</code>.</li>
      </ol>
      <div class="wmm-btn-row">
        <a class="wmm-btn wmm-btn--primary" href="https://wickermoney.dev/docs/self-hosting/quickstart">Open the full quickstart</a>
        <a class="wmm-btn wmm-btn--secondary" href="https://wickermoney.dev/docs/self-hosting/configuration">Configuration reference</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wmm-section">
    <div class="wmm-container">
      <h2>Before you commit to running this</h2>
      <p class="wmm-lede" style="max-width: 72ch;">
        Wicker Money is pre-1.0 with a single maintainer. Pre-1.0 means minor versions
        may still break things between releases — read
        <a href="https://wickermoney.dev/docs/self-hosting/upgrading">what to expect between upgrades</a>
        before you point it at data you can't afford to lose, and keep your own backups
        of the Postgres database regardless of what Wicker Money does or doesn't do.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
